content.text:
Good, 267 < 300. Now render-stage.js: stage-6 visibility + activeHopTarget + lazy LANES lookup.

Edits:
1. LANES: change map to lazy. Currently:
```js
const LANES = {
  'packet-req-left': $('packet-req-left'), ...
};
```
Replace with a list:
```js
// Lane ids looked up lazily: Stage 6's DNS/Router lanes are built by
// stage6-nodes.js at panel boot, after module load.
const LANE_IDS = [ 'packet-req-left', ..., 'packet-req-dns', 'packet-res-dns', 'packet-req-router', 'packet-res-router' ];
```
And renderHopHighlights:
```js
for (const id of LANE_IDS) {
  const node = document.getElementById(id);
  if (node) node.classList.toggle('lane-active', id === laneId);
}
```

2. renderStageTopology: hasWorkers = stage >= 5; hasDns/router stage >= 6; toggle node-dns, node-router, wire-browser-dns, wire-network-router. But careful: `$('node-dns')` may not exist at module load — renderStageTopology runs later (after boot) so getElementById works. Also stage < 6: hidden toggles for stage 1-5 → node-dns stays hidden ✓.

3. activeHopTarget stage 6: 
```js
if (snapshot.stage === 6) {
  const t = snapshot.trace ?? {};
  if (!t.hosted) { reuse stage-5 sync mapping with hop 1..8 }
  if (t.dnsStatus === 'NX') { 3-hop mapping }
  hosted 10-hop mapping
}
```
Stage-5 sync mapping from the existing stage-5 branch (non-async): owners {1 browser, 2 network, 3 lb, 4 db, 5 backendCard, 6 network, 7 browser, 8 worker}, lanes {1 req-left, 2 req-right, 3 req-lb, 4 dbLane, 5 res-cache, 6 res-right, 7 res-left, 8 res-worker}. For stage-6 host-less: same. I'll implement by falling through: change stage-5 branch condition to `stage === 5 || (stage === 6 && !snapshot.trace?.hosted)`. The existing branch computes asyncJob mapping too — for stage-6 host-less async POST /jobs works too (hosted POST example.com/jobs → hosted with async... hosted 10-hop async mapping needed for hops 6-10: db/queue hop (6): async → node-queue + packet-req-queue; serve (7): backend + packet-res-cache; network delivers (8): node-network res-right; browser received (9): browser res-left; worker commit (10): node-worker packet-res-db? In stage-5 async, hop 8 lane = packet-res-db and card node-worker. For hosted async hop 10 = worker commit → node-worker + packet-res-db.

Let me write a stage-6 branch explicitly:

```js
if (snapshot.stage === 6) {
  const t = snapshot.trace ?? {};
  const backendCard = t.targetServer === '10.12' ? 'node-webserver-2' : 'node-webserver';
  const dbLane = t.dbOp === 'WRITE' ? 'packet-req-db' : 'packet-res-db';
  if (!t.hosted) {
    // identical to stage-5 mapping (sync + async)
    const owners = t.asyncJob ? {...} : {...};  // copy of stage-5
    const lanes = t.asyncJob ? {...} : {...};
    return { cardId: owners[t.hop] ?? 'node-browser', laneId: lanes[t.hop] ?? 'packet-req-left' };
  }
  if (t.dnsStatus === 'NX') {
    const owners = { 1: 'node-browser', 2: 'node-dns', 3: 'node-dns' };
    const lanes = { 1: 'packet-req-left', 2: 'packet-req-dns', 3: 'packet-res-dns' };
    return { cardId: owners[t.hop] ?? 'node-dns', laneId: lanes[t.hop] ?? 'packet-req-dns' };
  }
  // hosted 10-hop
  const owners = t.asyncJob
    ? { 1:'node-browser', 2:'node-dns', 3:'node-dns', 4:'node-network', 5:'node-lb', 6:'node-queue', 7:backendCard, 8:'node-network', 9:'node-browser', 10:'node-worker' }
    : { 1:'node-browser', 2:'node-dns', 3:'node-dns', 4:'node-network', 5:'node-lb', 6:'node-db', 7:backendCard, 8:'node-network', 9:'node-browser', 10:'node-worker' };
  const lanes = t.asyncJob
    ? { 1:'packet-req-left', 2:'packet-req-dns', 3:'packet-res-dns', 4:'packet-req-right', 5:'packet-req-lb', 6:'packet-req-queue', 7:'packet-res-cache', 8:'packet-res-right', 9:'packet-res-left', 10:'packet-res-db' }
    : { 1:'packet-req-left', 2:'packet-req-dns', 3:'packet-res-dns', 4:'packet-req-right', 5:'packet-req-lb', 6:dbLane, 7:'packet-res-cache', 8:'packet-res-right', 9:'packet-res-left', 10:'packet-res-worker' };
  return { cardId: owners[t.hop] ?? 'node-browser', laneId: lanes[t.hop] ?? 'packet-req-left' };
}
```

To avoid duplicating stage-5's mapping, restructure: extract `stage5HopOwners(t)` returning {owners, lanes} then use for stage 5 and stage-6 host-less. Let me refactor the stage-5 branch into a helper above activeHopTarget:

```js
function stage5HopMap(snapshot) { ... returns {cardId, laneId} }
```
Actually simpler: at top of activeHopTarget:
```js
const hop = snapshot.trace?.hop ?? 0;
if (snapshot.stage === 5 || (snapshot.stage === 6 && !snapshot.trace?.hosted)) {
  ...existing stage-5 body verbatim (it checks snapshot.trace?.asyncJob etc.)...
}
```
That's minimal — the existing body uses `snapshot.trace?.targetServer` and `dbOp`, fine for stage 6 host-less. So just extend the condition. Then add the stage-6 hosted/NX branch before it.

